# The "Only my voice" speaker model is NOT committed (cloud-builds step 4, 2026-11-20).
# A cloud build fetches the OFFICIAL file from the URL below and checks its size and sha256
# (.github/scripts/fetch_speaker_model.sh). The laptop's copy is one byte shorter and has another
# sha256 (c5915837...), so its origin is unproven and it is never committed.
#
# release_ok stays "no" until the official file has been tried on the phone with the enrolled
# voiceprint (re-enrolled if needed) and found to tell the owner's voice from others as well as the
# laptop copy does. While it is "no", a cloud APK build stops before building: no APK ships without
# a speaker model, and none ships with an untried one. Flip it to "yes" in its own reviewed commit.
#
# Source: k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx release "speaker-recongition-models" (sic), the ONNX export of
# 3D-Speaker's ERes2Net (English, VoxCeleb, 16 kHz). size and sha256 are the ones GitHub reports for
# that release asset (asset digest, read 2026-11-20; the asset was last updated 2026-11-19).
# Licence: Apache-2.0 (modelscope/3D-Speaker and k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx); notice in
# app/src/main/assets/speaker/README.md. The licence text is fetched from 3D-Speaker at a pinned
# commit and checked by its git blob id (the standard Apache-2.0 text).
path=speaker/3dspeaker_speech_eres2net_sv_en_voxceleb_16k.onnx
url=https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/speaker-recongition-models/3dspeaker_speech_eres2net_sv_en_voxceleb_16k.onnx
bytes=26485264
sha256=c4947caf150b8502fdd75bbe4089b971ab1ec42e90ee3ba547faca2cde44d9ee
license_path=licenses/3dspeaker-eres2net-Apache-2.0.txt
license_url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelscope/3D-Speaker/b6ea24f428a178c02b7ef9d6900569050448c8a1/LICENSE
license_git_blob=261eeb9e9f8b2b4b0d119366dda99c6fd7d35c64
release_ok=no
